# Files the Vercel CLI uploads. Without this, Vercel falls back to .gitignore,
# but `public/` is treated as a static-asset directory and gets uploaded
# regardless — including `public/search-index.json`, the reduced DEV index that
# `predev` writes.
#
# That file shadows the real one in production: Vercel serves prerendered routes
# plus whatever is in public/, never out/. So a stale section-less index would
# silently kill section search online while the build log still reports the
# correct entry count. Do not delete this file, and add any other generated file
# placed in public/ here too.
public/search-index.json

# Never deploy a local build: Vercel runs its own `npm run build`, and shipping
# out/ risks serving stale HTML that predates the build.
out
